{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>A voice of the shepherds</b> — they are the kings, and their glory is the Hasmoneans." "<b>A voice of the roar of young lions</b> — for the young lion is king of the beasts, and the word כפירים serves on account of another, like כסאך אלהים (Psalms 45:7), which is כסאך כסא אלהים, and likewise here: כי שדד כפיר (Jeremiah 49:19), in which the Jordan gloried in him, for no man could cross the Jordan out of fear of him. And if we interpret it that the Jordan dried up, it has no sense. And Yefet said: for the glory of Israel was destroyed across the Jordan. This too is sound in my eyes."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:43.747772125Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}